## Scope

This workshop covered the design and application of fluid antenna systems (FAS) for 6G wireless communications. Its scope included both movable and non-movable flexible antenna structures and how their reconfigurability can improve wireless link performance. It also addressed how FAS can be combined with other wireless technologies, including massive MIMO, intelligent reflecting surfaces, full-duplex communications, and terahertz communications.

## Discussion Topics

- **Flexible and reconfigurable antenna designs** — Movable and non-movable antenna structures for fluid antenna systems.
- **Spatial multiplexing and massive MIMO** — The use of antenna reconfigurability to improve spatial multiplexing.
- **Reconfigurable intelligent surfaces and beamforming** — Beamforming design for systems that combine fluid antennas with intelligent reflecting surfaces.
- **Integration with other wireless technologies** — Applications of fluid antennas in full-duplex and terahertz communications.

